# Shuttle house style. Derived from the code that already exists, not imposed
# on it: Google style is the base because the include grouping, 80-column
# limit, attached braces, left-aligned pointers (`void* base`) and
# short-if-on-one-line habits in this tree already match it. Four deviations,
# each observed in the source:
#
#   IndentWidth 4              — the tree indents 4, Google's default is 2.
#   AccessModifierOffset -3    — yields ` public:` at one space, as written.
#   AlwaysBreakBeforeMultiline
#     Strings: false           — the printf/snprintf format strings in bench/
#                                and tools/ stay on the call's first line.
#   IncludeIsMainRegex '$'     — do NOT treat foo.hpp as the "main header" of
#                                foo_test.cpp; tests here include the unit
#                                under test inside the normal project block.
#
# Running clang-format over the tree is very close to a no-op (see
# CONTRIBUTING.md). Reformat only what you touch; a whole-tree sweep would
# bury real history under noise.
Language: Cpp
BasedOnStyle: Google
IndentWidth: 4
AccessModifierOffset: -3
AlwaysBreakBeforeMultilineStrings: false
IncludeIsMainRegex: '$'
